     <DESCRIPTION>Protocols: Protonema were grown for 7days on PpNH4 medium (F. Charlot et Al, Physcomitrium patens protoplasting and protoplast transfection, in: K. Wang, F. Zhang (Eds.), Methods Mol. Biol. (Clifton, N.J.)-Protoplast Technol., Springer Nature, 2022: p. In Press). Plants were cultured as described previously in (Cove DJ et al, 2009) Plants were transformed with Crispr-Cas9 as previously described in (Collonnier C. et al, 2017) Genomics DNA was extracted from 1.5 g of fresh protonema. DNA samples were extracted using the NucleoSpin™ PlantII Kit (Macherey-Nagel) as described by the manufacturer. Kapa Hyper Prep (index 12 bases)</DESCRIPTION>
